==Strategy==
Since it's the first stage of Into the Future, it's easy. Even if the Shibalien overpowers your troops, he has a moderate attack rate and a Single Target attack, meaning you can stall him with [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Cat]] and [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Wall Cat]] and hit him with [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Sexy Legs Cat]], [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]] and other longer-ranged attackers. Spamming [[Cow Cat (Normal Cat)|Giraffe Cats]] is another way to take him down easily. It is highly recommended to use [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Castaway Cat]]

Once the Shibalien is dead, the remaining peons pose no threat and you can claim victory.

==Trivia==
*This stage is most likely underwater because the intro to this chapter says the [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Aliens]] sunk Japan. However, on the in-game map, some of Japan appears above water.
*Unlike other [[Into the Future]] stages, Japan's base is not a modified version of its [[Empire of Cats]] counterpart. In the [[Japan (Empire of Cats)|Japan]] stage of Empire of Cats, the base was a [[wikipedia:Maiko|''maiko'']] in front of [[wikipedia:Kinkaku-ji|Kinkaku-ji]], but here it's the sunken ruin of the [[wikipedia:Tokyo Tower|Tokyo Tower]], which originally appeared in [[Bermuda (Empire of Cats)|stage 35]] of [[Nyanko Daisensou|BCJP]].

